--TEST--
`Core\Command::run` refuses a case the union did not name, even though its enum declares it — `rule:tooling/commands-are-compiled`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The subset is a bound and not decoration. `Quiet` is a case of the same enum
// and spells a word the whole-enum conversion takes
// (`command-run-converts-an-enum-argument-by-its-case-name`), so a filter that
// kept every pair would answer this line identically while quietly handing the
// handler a value outside its declared type — which is the one thing the
// conversion exists to make unwritable.
//
// `run` prints its usage page to standard error, which a case does not read, so
// the refusal is asserted as § 6's usage status and by the handler never
// running: a converted `Quiet` would have printed a line before `run` returned.
enum Level: uint {
    Quiet = 1,
    Warn = 10,
    Error = 20,
}

class Logs {
    #[Core\Command(name: "emit", about: "Write one line at a level")]
    public static function emit(Level::Warn|Level::Error $level): uint {
        echo "level: ", $level as uint, "\n";
        return 0;
    }
}

echo "status: ", Core\Command::run(), "\n";
--ARGS--
emit
Quiet
--EXPECT--
status: 2
